From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lavc/rkmppenc: validate the DRM descriptor before importing
 it

rkmpp_set_drm_frame() read desc->layers[0], that layer's planes[0] and
planes[1], and desc->objects[0] without checking any of the counts that say
those exist, and without checking where the planes actually live.

Three consequences, all reachable from a producer that shapes its
descriptor differently to this build's own hwcontext:

 - nb_layers or nb_planes below what is indexed reads uninitialised
   descriptor memory and encodes from it;
 - planes[0].pitch of zero makes `layer->planes[1].offset / stride` a
   division by zero, which is SIGFPE, not an error return;
 - a frame whose planes live in more than one dma-buf imported only
   object 0, silently encoding whatever occupied the chroma offset in it.

Check the counts before indexing, reject a non-positive stride, and reject
a multi-object frame with ENOSYS -- MPP is handed a single buffer here, so
that shape is unsupported rather than malformed.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavcodec/rkmppenc.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/rkmppenc.c b/libavcodec/rkmppenc.c
index 09501f0..a8d9db5 100644
--- a/libavcodec/rkmppenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/rkmppenc.c
@@ -377,9 +377,32 @@ static int rkmpp_set_hw_frame(AVCodecContext *avctx, MppFrame frame)
 
 
     const AVDRMFrameDescriptor *desc = (AVDRMFrameDescriptor *)ctx->frame->data[0];
-    const AVDRMLayerDescriptor *layer = &desc->layers[0];
+    const AVDRMLayerDescriptor *layer;
+
+    /* The descriptor is externally supplied -- a producer other than this
+     * build's own hwcontext may shape it differently -- so its counts are
+     * checked before its arrays are read. */
+    if (!desc || desc->nb_objects < 1 || desc->nb_layers < 1)
+        return AVERROR(EINVAL);
+
+    layer = &desc->layers[0];
+    if (layer->nb_planes < 2)
+        return AVERROR(EINVAL);
+
+    /* MPP is handed one dma-buf, so every plane must live in the object that
+     * is handed over. Importing object 0 for a frame whose chroma is in
+     * object 1 encodes whatever else happens to be at that offset. */
+    for (int i = 0; i < layer->nb_planes; i++) {
+        if (layer->planes[i].object_index != 0) {
+            av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "DRM frames split across multiple objects "
+                   "are not supported\n");
+            return AVERROR(ENOSYS);
+        }
+    }
 
     int stride = layer->planes[0].pitch;
+    if (stride <= 0)
+        return AVERROR(EINVAL);
     int vertical = layer->planes[1].offset / stride;
     if (stride != ctx->mpp_stride || vertical != ctx->mpp_height) {
         // Update stride info
